{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/118248-\u200bpointless-but-fun-exigent-mechanics-speculation","id":118248,"title":"\u200bPointless but fun Exigent Mechanics Speculation!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-23T21:20:11-07:00","id":118248,"title":"\u200bPointless but fun Exigent Mechanics Speculation!","content":"So I am 100% for the Exigents. The whole idea seems ridiculously cool and I am excited to see how it will work out. However I have no idea how it will work out.<br /> <br /> One whole hard back to help you make your own type of unique exalt. I assume there has to be some underlying mechanic introduced in the book for people like me. That is people with lots of ideas but suck at balancing and executing those ideas; I am terrible at game design. Additionally we know it does not use point buy so that is interesting.<br /> So let\u2019s pointlessly speculate on how Exigents work Mechanically.<br /> <br /> I guess I\u2019ll get it started:<br /> <br /> I am going to guess that maybe all Exigents share the same excellency charms which might not be attribute or ability based but theme based like Infernals. The themes being those of the god that the exigency drives from.<br /> <br /> I am also going to guess that Exigents can be either ability or attribute based. Unless the designers really pull something out of their hat and create a new paradigm just for Exigents which might actually be an interesting idea. Most Exigents probably won\u2019t have castes so instead of having favored skills or attributes they will have some other factor.<br /> <br /> Perhaps how it will work is there will be basic charm \u2018skeletons\u2019 with additional options that add in \u2018meat\u2019 both of which can be flavored appropriately with text. Then this base Skeleton can be added onto with custom charms.<br /> <br /> What are all of your ideas on how this might work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2302,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","user":"Snakesandsuns","date":". 04-24-2014, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T22:58:32-07:00","id":118274,"title":"","content":"I could easily see that working well for the Exigents. It allows you to create charms but then the players can customize them to create their own, unique charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T14:52:38-07:00","id":118651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/118248-\u200bpointless-but-fun-exigent-mechanics-speculation#post118248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am also going to guess that Exigents can be either ability or attribute based. Unless the designers really pull something out of their hat and create a new paradigm just for Exigents which might actually be an interesting idea. Most Exigents probably won\u2019t have castes so instead of having favored skills or attributes they will have some other factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we'd be doing a disservice to players and Storytellers who want to make Exigents with weird, unorthodox Charmsets if we didn't give y'all at least one Exigent Charmset that was entirely unprecedented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T16:15:38-07:00","id":118730,"title":"","content":"The way I understand it, there will be no underlying mechanic, just a set of guidelines and tips on how to make your Exigent balanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T17:09:51-07:00","id":118774,"title":"","content":"That seems to be the way of it. And one need look no further than Vance's comment to understand that there will be no small number of example Exigents in the book. Each Exigent really is a completely distinct Exalt type unto itself.<br /> <br /> Many quotes on Exigents from the EX3 Team can be found in <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalts#Exigents\" target=\"_blank\">the Exigent section</a> on the What We Know Wiki. Have a few from John over the past... year or so...?:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Two Exigents] would be two completely different Exalts, like joining a Solar and a Lunar.<br /> <br /> They range as far afield as you can imagine.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> We have put a lot of thought into how to pull this off, and so a part of the Exigents hardback will be dedicated to building your own.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Exigents are unique Exalts. The difference between the classics and the Exigents are that Exigents are based on a variety of gods and can produce really strange results, some of which are difficult to trace back to any kind of spirit. Their powers/natures/builds are as varied and crazy as you can imagine.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> I formulated the Exigents to cover any Exalt you could come up with, with any kind of crazy Charm or mechanical schema imaginable.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Questions like &quot;I wonder if the Exigents will have an apotheosis path like the Devil-Tigers?&quot; and &quot;How good will the Exigents be at Evocations?&quot; tell me that you are thinking of them as one kind of Exalt. They're not.<br /> <br /> Every Exigent is unique and works differently. You can have an Exigent who has an apotheosis path and you can have an Exigent who is all about Evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T17:21:24-07:00","id":118784,"title":"","content":"Yeah, as I understand it, Exigents are supposed to have no more in common with each other than they do with Solars or Dragonblooded or Abyssals or... you get the point.<br /> <br /> So it's more likely that you'd have guidelines for &quot;they should have some kind of Excellency&quot; (if Excellencies are still a thing), and then an exploration of the advantages and disadvantages of various Excellency models (Lunars get broader application but a lower ceiling, etc.), and &quot;they should have areas of focus and areas of non-focus. For the latter, with an Exigent there's no real reason to assume they can develop that kind of Charm at all [or 'they get the option of developing really minimal power charms'].<br /> <br /> It's hard to say without knowing what a 3e Charmset even looks like...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T17:25:55-07:00","id":118791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/118248-\u200bpointless-but-fun-exigent-mechanics-speculation?p=118651#post118651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think we'd be doing a disservice to players and Storytellers who want to make Exigents with weird, unorthodox Charmsets if we didn't give y'all at least one Exigent Charmset that was entirely unprecedented.</div> </div> </div> </div> Confirmed: Madame Marthesine's Exalts' Charms are based entirely on the contents of their pockets in their moment of need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T18:47:56-07:00","id":118841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/118248-\u200bpointless-but-fun-exigent-mechanics-speculation?p=118651#post118651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we'd be doing a disservice to players and Storytellers who want to make Exigents with weird, unorthodox Charmsets if we didn't give y'all at least one Exigent Charmset that was entirely unprecedented.</div> </div> </div> </div>so its going to be possible to make charms with only essence like the old infernals, i dont know whats the popular opinion on that but i leve it, it felt a lot like magic powers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T20:10:54-07:00","id":118896,"title":"","content":"Anyone wanna speculate on possible unprecedented Charmsets? I'll start:<br /> <br /> - A charmset with no requisites at all. No charm trees, just a gigantic bag of tricks that don't really advance into more powerful tricks and further power comes from various synergies between different tricks<br /> <br /> - A Charmset in which you just pay experience to determine how many Charms you know, but which Charms you have at any given time are determined at random each day from a pool of all possible charms you could have from your Charmset (possibly per Ability or Attribute or whatever, so that you could at least trust to always have, say, 5 melee Charms or something)<br /> <br /> - A Charmset composed of minor effects, but all of them permanent. Only a few even have some possible uses that cost any Essence.<br /> <br /> - A Charmset that starts out with really weak charms, but each new charm you buy on the same tree unlocks a new effect or increases the effect of all other charms on that tree<br /> <br /> - A consumable Charmset. Charms can be &quot;consumed&quot; or &quot;expended&quot; to generate a much greater effect than usual, but then that Charm becomes unvailable for a long time. For a more extreme version, ultra-powerful Charms that can only be used once (generally one scene) then you lose that Charm. You get your XP refunded and with training time can learn another Charm, but you can't relearn a charm you already used.<br /> <br /> -A living/sentient/aware/whatever Charmset that can activate itself and has its own ideas and opinions. You better make sure it has good intimacies toward you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T21:23:54-07:00","id":118928,"title":"","content":"Ooh, those are awesome, danelsan! ^__^ Very creative! Especially the last two, kind of stretching the idea of what Charms can be.<br /> <br /> Here are three you inspired in me, much as the first plays off your last one quite a bit.<br /> <br /> - A Charmset in which every Charm (or every root Charm) is a living creature/person. Each follow-up Charm can advance these other entities' powers and capabilities. They may or may not also provide some passive bonus to the Exalt (e.g. Not-Charizard learned a passive flame aura, so his Trainer Exalt is now super-resistant to fire!). It may be that only some number of Charm familiars may be &quot;active&quot; at once to prevent numerical abuse. And/Or maybe some other factors to consider in the case of Charm familiars getting killed. Depending on particulars, can represent an Exalt who's all about familiars, Pokemon/Digimon, Fate/StayNight, a Devil-Tiger's Soul hierarchy, and plenty else.<br /> <br /> - A Charmset in which every Charm is, or allows one to easily make, an object. Instead of being about becoming a great user of weapons, Melee would be all about creating melee weapons with interesting and distinct qualities. Higher levels might even produce (limited) artifact gear, possibly even with Evocation-like powers of their own. While dangerous enough if the Exalt uses this stuff personally (and perhaps with special bonuses if the Exalt does), the true power is in giving this stuff to other people. Be it equipping an army or another Exalt with special equipment or offering tomes of difficult knowledge conveyed very clearly to educate the populace or help another Exalt master something difficult, this Exigent is a clear force multiplier.<br /> <br /> - The Exigent develops an amazing tie to the land of his or her patron, and the Charmset reflects this. Charms define less personal capacities of the Exalt and more the qualities and ways of manipulating the locale, exerting influence over inhabitants (primarily through geographical features and local wildlife), and maybe even drawing off the land for personal power. Some Charms might create geographic features, or help the rivers grow pristine and filled with fish. A mountain might stand so majestic that those who behold it begin developing an Intimacy toward the land, while other Charms might make the animals desire to protect/serve the land and make them unusually powerful when doing so. Charms in turn for allowing use of Intimacies toward the land as though they were Intimacies toward oneself would be natural outgrowths, as would commanding beasts or geographical features to act or attack as one wishes.<br /> <br /> At the extreme end, Charms for great personal power (unusual for this set) might not cost motes (or at least not <i>just</i> motes), but would allow one to draw on the power of parts of the land at the cost of diminishing them (e.g. &quot;I am swift as the coursing river!&quot; for a scene might also mean the mighty river becomes less mighty; time and effort can mend it, but an especially tough situation can leave the land suffering at least as much as the Exalt). The Exaltation may ensure its bearer reincarnates as a person (or even animal?) born on the land, though this blessing may be thwarted if the land is sufficiently brought to ruin. There may be interesting possibilities if the land becomes, encompasses, or comes to encompass -- no reason it can't grow! -- a Shadowland, Wyld Zone, or other oddity.<br /> <br /> EDIT: One who wanted to play Sim City as an Alchemical Petropolis or Metropolis, or an Infernal/other entity with some sort of world body, could also find value in this idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Man, that third one just kept going. 04-25-2014, 12:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T21:47:45-07:00","id":118935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/118248-\u200bpointless-but-fun-exigent-mechanics-speculation?p=118651#post118651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we'd be doing a disservice to players and Storytellers who want to make Exigents with weird, unorthodox Charmsets if we didn't give y'all at least one Exigent Charmset that was entirely unprecedented.</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess is that what you will give us in the Exigent book is a bunch of blank charms, that are half finished templates and then we finish them off. A good example is savage worlds/necessary evil spells/power where you just pick them and flesh them out. With rules on adjustment of minimums required, power drawbacks and flaws that not only create balance but insure that no two powers are alike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T21:51:17-07:00","id":118936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/118248-\u200bpointless-but-fun-exigent-mechanics-speculation?p=118928#post118928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh, those are awesome, danelsan! ^__^ Very creative! Especially the last two, kind of stretching the idea of what Charms can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I like yours as well ^__^ Exigents and Evocations have inspired plenty of ideas in me. I hope I'll be able to develop a decent system mastery to translate them all into reasonably useable mechanics once EX3 is out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/118248-\u200bpointless-but-fun-exigent-mechanics-speculation?p=118928#post118928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- A Charmset in which every Charm (or every root Charm) is a living creature/person. Each follow-up Charm can advance these other entities' powers and capabilities. They may or may not also provide some passive bonus to the Exalt (e.g. Not-Charizard learned a passive flame aura, so his Trainer Exalt is now super-resistant to fire!). It may be that only some number of Charm familiars may be &quot;active&quot; at once to prevent numerical abuse. And/Or maybe some other factors to consider in the case of Charm familiars getting killed. Depending on particulars, can represent an Exalt who's all about familiars, Pokemon/Digimon, Fate/StayNight, a Devil-Tiger's Soul hierarchy, and plenty else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually had a vaguely similar idea I didn't post then because I cut the post short due to some stuff I had to do away from the computer. The main difference is that my idea was more based on having either the creature or the power at any given time. That is, you could have the &quot;Electric Rodent&quot; Charm tree, for instance, and either use it to summon Not-Pikachu, or to have it fuse with you, granting electric powers to yourself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/118248-\u200bpointless-but-fun-exigent-mechanics-speculation?p=118928#post118928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the extreme end, Charms for unusual personal power (unusual for this set, anyway) might not cost motes (or at least not <i>just</i> motes), but would allow one to draw on the power of parts of the land at the cost of diminishing them (e.g. &quot;I am swift as the coursing river!&quot; for a scene might also mean the mighty river becomes less mighty, much as time can mend it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just avoid using, if at all possible, the Charm &quot;I am mysterious as the dark side of the moon&quot;, unless you want Luna pissed off at you for diminishing the moon...<br /> <br /> ... And now I have an idea for a Charmset in which every Charm Tree comes from a song. Not unprecedented, though - that is not too far from Sidereal Trees following the lines of a Sutra, though of course you can always compose new songs and derive Charms from them, while Sidereals keep restricted to their &quot;Saving the world with a hammer, 2 pounds of rice and a rubber duck&quot; theme.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T11:37:13-07:00","id":122531,"title":"","content":"Speaking of funky charmsets, has anyone thought of alchemical-esque charms evolving from either moonsilver artifact tattoos or Genesis-based symbiotes?<br /> <br /> Also, would <a href=\"http://www.demonhunterkain.com/comic/dhk-chapter-3-page-3/\" target=\"_blank\">these guys</a> count as a brand of Exigents? Just curious on your opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T12:22:49-07:00","id":122568,"title":"","content":"I just thought, it could be pretty interesting playing an Exigent of Lytek the god of exaltations. Maybe you'd be a chronicler of heroes type or something, it'd be a fun character nonetheless i'm sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amateur drawsmith","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2847-thatsmellygoblin","name":"ThatSmellyGoblin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2847_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T12:24:56-07:00","id":122570,"title":"","content":"A big deal with Exigents is their singular natures. The sacrifice required to make them means you generally wouldn't have multiple Exigents of the same theme running around (indeed, most Exigents are the only one of their kind in all of history). I don't know the details of that webcomic, but seeing as there's apparently an entire order of demon-hunters, it's probably closer to one of the main splats' roles in the fiction. Granted, if God and His Servant initally only created a single demon-hunter (who then somehow went on to produce more of them) and were left severely diminished by the act, it'd fit fairly well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T15:43:37-07:00","id":122717,"title":"","content":"First Exigent I think I want to play's patron god will be a local goddess of duels, romantic conflicts, and romantic conquests. It think it might be interesting to see what kind of character I could generate off those themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T19:12:29-07:00","id":122852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/118248-\u200bpointless-but-fun-exigent-mechanics-speculation?p=122717#post122717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First Exigent I think I want to play's patron god will be a local goddess of duels, romantic conflicts, and romantic conquests. It think it might be interesting to see what kind of character I could generate off those themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give her a rose motif. When she fights a duel for the sake of a Major or Defining Tie, she has the power to draw a magical sword out of her loved one's heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T19:23:21-07:00","id":122859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mewtarthio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/118248-\u200bpointless-but-fun-exigent-mechanics-speculation?p=122570#post122570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A big deal with Exigents is their singular natures. The sacrifice required to make them means you generally wouldn't have multiple Exigents of the same theme running around (indeed, most Exigents are the only one of their kind in all of history).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about the &quot;most,&quot; but there absolutely do exist Exigents whose Exaltation can reincarnate/transfer/replicate, or Exigents who are one of many created by a single deity. The &quot;one and done&quot; Exigent model is very useful, but having <i>just</i> that model would be an unuseful limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T19:49:48-07:00","id":122877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/118248-\u200bpointless-but-fun-exigent-mechanics-speculation?p=122859#post122859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure about the &quot;most,&quot; but there absolutely do exist Exigents whose Exaltation can reincarnate/transfer/replicate, or Exigents who are one of many created by a single deity. The &quot;one and done&quot; Exigent model is very useful, but having <i>just</i> that model would be an unuseful limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>What that book comes out, I think I'm going to try to build an Exigent version of Star Trek Trills and one that is sort of a Highlander style thing, where there are several exaltations that reincarnate separately, but they can be stolen and absorbed by someone that already has one, eventually recreating a super powerful version of the Spirit that originally built them. I imagine I'll have other ideas when I read it, but those are the ones I've [strike]stolen[/strike] thought of so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T19:51:18-07:00","id":122879,"title":"","content":"....Ok, can you do strike out text on this board?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T19:52:50-07:00","id":122882,"title":"","content":"Also, some kind of Magical Girl Exigent would be fun. Especially if I can send her off with a team of Sidereals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T21:03:38-07:00","id":122916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mewtarthio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/118248-\u200bpointless-but-fun-exigent-mechanics-speculation?p=122852#post122852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Give her a rose motif. When she fights a duel for the sake of a Major or Defining Tie, she has the power to draw a magical sword out of her loved one's heart.</div> </div> </div> </div>One problem with your Utena parallel. It will be a guy. Otherwise the rose theme, drawing a sword from a loved ones heart (that is a cool charm in it's self). Not sure if it's the equivalent to the Solar/Dragon Blooded &quot;form blazing sword&quot; or the &quot;Store a item in elsewhere&quot; charm but my elsewhere pocket is in the heart of my lover. Either way, needing them there....that's pretty big and can lead to it's own problems.<br /> <br /> Probably a storage portal. I think I like that better. Man I'm getting all kinds of cool ideas off this theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 05-01-2014, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}